2026-09-11T20:00:00.001Z note THREE cross-vendor review rounds by hand (claude wrote, codex reviewed), so no manifest records them. Fifteen findings across the three, every one real, every one fixed. Round 1: a leaked subscription on disconnect, an unhandled rejection in the detached forwarder, a bind promise that could never settle on EADDRINUSE, a stop route ignoring unknown fields the start route refused, a classifier reporting an undiagnosed failure as "no such ticket", and NO TEST OPENING THE WEBSOCKET AT ALL. Round 2: the retention default and the backpressure bound — both explicit requirements of the ticket body — simply not implemented, the missed send outside the guarded task, no-such-flow matching a phrase nobody writes, and a test of mine that asserted only that the run still existed. Round 3: four more, all the same shape — new behaviour with no test that could fail on it.
2026-09-11T20:00:00.002Z note the honest assessment: the fast track saved a requirements gate and a chore gate, and the review loop it replaced was done by hand and less well. Three rounds each found real defects and the rounds were not converging the way a bounded loop does; a fourth might still find things. Recorded so the next fast-track decision is made with this rather than with an impression.
